      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `UTF_16BE` and `UTF_16LE` are not equal to each other (symmetrically). Let me write an improved, more understandable version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version renames the test method to `test08_differentEndianBOMsAreNotEqual` for clarity, uses descriptive variable names (`utf16BigEndian`/`utf16LittleEndian` instead of `byteOrderMark0`/`byteOrderMark1`), adds a Javadoc comment explaining the byte-sequence rationale, and includes assertion messages that make failures self-explanatory — all while preserving the exact same method calls, arguments, and expected outcomes."
